{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Sojourn in this land.</b> He commanded him not to go outside the Land. And the reason for this is that he had been sanctified on Mount Moriah and was a whole burnt offering, and therefore He warned him never to leave the Holy Land and not to become defiled in the land of the nations." "<b>And</b> that He expressed the language of the command in the term גור (sojourn), after He had said to him כון (dwell), was in order to allude to him concerning גור אריה — the lion's whelp — which is the fear of Isaac. And one should not wonder if the fear of Isaac was upon him on the day of the Binding (akedah), since he saw there the form of a lion upon the altar, from what our Rabbis of blessed memory expounded (Genesis 27:33): ״ויחרד יצחק חרדה וגו׳״ — Isaac trembled with a great trembling, etc. — two tremblings did he tremble: one upon the altar and one here."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:15:16.479256884Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}